issue-orchestrator tech-lead pattern registry

{"entries":[{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-80985","classification":{"area":"","diagnosis":"","fix_class":""},"expires_at":"2026-10-09T08:00:38.537483+00:00","issue_number":null,"lifecycle":[],"observation_ids":[],"pending":{"area":"tech-lead-observability","body_observation_id":"20261009-065625Z-3d890e7ad4394e6b82fc24a1d4b4f3fc:tech-lead-2:A3","diagnosis":"**Causal mechanism.** The board snapshot reads open pattern case files from the tech-lead anchor scan (`control/tech_lead_anchor_scan.py:72-89`). That scan comes from `discover_open_tech_lead_anchor_issues` (`control/health_review_trigger.py:213-243`), which keeps only issues carrying `config.filtering.label`. The scoping is correct for anchors: it stops one run from launching another run's review. But case-file issues are durable, engine-wide ledger issues and do not carry a run's filter label. In any engine with `filtering.label` set, `case_files` and `area_signals` are therefore always empty, and `tech-lead-board.md` says \"Open pattern case files: None\". Meanwhile the authority ledger (`tech_lead_authority.sqlite` `tech_lead_patterns`) holds live case files. This is the same masking class as #6963, which found the same blindness under a one-shot launch. The trigger here is filter-label scope.\n\n**Observation (io-pilot, health review #9241, 2026-10-09).** Snapshot `case_files=[]` and `area_signals=[]`. The ledger has active patterns with OPEN issues: e2e-suite-chronic-red #7237, search-api-budget-exhaustion #7235, review-exchange-restart-rederives-reviewer-verdict #7084, and needs_human tech-lead-dedup-redirect-gate-orphans-offgrant-evidence #7037. The ledger also disagrees with GitHub the other way: it lists #7319 and #7321 as `active`, but GitHub closed both on 2026-09-27.\n\n**Suggested fix (code).** Build the snapshot's `case_files`, `area_signals` and `recent_shipped_fixes` from the authority ledger, joined to the issue state the scan already fetched, independent of anchor scope and launch shape. This is #6963's proposed direction, and it covers both triggers. Reconcile ledger disposition with GitHub closure, so a case file closed on GitHub stops reading active. Never present an unobserved signal as an empty list: when the source could not be read, say \"not observed\". Regression test: a filter-label engine's snapshot lists a ledger case file whose issue lacks the filter label.","fix_class":"code","idempotency_marker":"<!-- issue-orchestrator:tech-lead-case-file:v1:d98836b48ddb483197d2580599400168747a586c10ec29f7f6a8831f552fbca2 -->","signature":"board-snapshot-masks-case-file-ledger","title":"Pattern case file: board-snapshot-masks-case-file-ledger"},"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"89b346863b154e90b920d2652877c516","signature":"board-snapshot-masks-case-file-ledger"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"","diagnosis":"","fix_class":""},"expires_at":"1970-01-01T00:00:00+00:00","issue_number":7237,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"active","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7237"],"reason":"The case was freshly reconciled and still represents unresolved E2E signal health rather than completed work.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:e2e-suite-chronic-red"}],"observation_ids":["6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:registration","6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:duplicate-6961","6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:duplicate-6978"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"migration:c47e4f3d0b5fc055","signature":"e2e-suite-chronic-red"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"run-ownership","diagnosis":"**Signature:** the host suspends, the engine's own run hold expires while it is\nfrozen, and on wake the lapse is interpreted as a rival owner - so a\nsingle-engine orchestrator declares its own runs lost and kills its own live\nsessions.\n\n**Mechanism**\n\nRun holds are 15 minutes and are renewed from the tick loop. A host sleep stops\nthe loop without stopping wall clock. On wake, `tech_lead_run_ownership` compares\na now-expired hold against wall time, concludes the hold lapsed, and\n`tech_lead_run_admission` terminates the active session and withdraws queued\nwork - the same consequence path as a genuine peer takeover, despite there being\nno peer.\n\n**Occurrence (2026-08-17)**\n\nForward tick gaps in EDT: 01:13:09->01:45:52, 01:45:52->02:02:19,\n02:02:22->02:37:47, 02:37:49->02:50:24, 02:50:24->03:06:23, 03:06:23->03:14:05,\n03:14:10->03:29:35 - roughly 135 minutes of suspension against a 15-minute lease.\nAt 06:37:48Z, runs 6926/6971/6989/7005/7014/7024/7040 were declared lost in a\nsingle second (`orchestrator.log:605991-606003`) and #6926's live tech-lead\nsession was terminated (`606004`). The renewal attempt one second earlier logged\n`expires in -4264.7s` at INFO with no warning, no event, and no alarm (`605988`).\n\n**Compounding: the clock itself moved.** Between `[LOOP] Iteration 4167` and\n`4168` the host shifted **-3h** (EDT->PDT), so every naive-local-clock duration\nspanning that boundary is fiction. Completion records are stamped with naive\nlocal time: `completion-coder.json` records `2026-08-17T00:56:42.044031` while\nits sibling validation record records `2026-08-17T07:56:42.105269+00:00` for the\nsame instant.\n\n**Suggested fix**\n\nDetect suspension explicitly (monotonic-vs-wall divergence across a tick) and\ntreat a self-lapse as \"reacquire or stop cleanly\", never as peer takeover. Stamp\nall durable records in UTC with an explicit offset, and raise the negative-expiry\nlog to WARNING with an event. Related surface: #7035 files the same symptom under\na load hypothesis; suspension is the confirmed cause here.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:38:24.097049+00:00","issue_number":7082,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"shipped","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7118","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7082"],"reason":"Run deadlines and owner backoff now distinguish host suspension from live elapsed work.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:host-suspend-lapses-run-ownership-lease"}],"observation_ids":["20260817-073208Z:coding-1:A9","20260820-010159Z:coding-1:A5"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"02a65ef19e35422e9a58cec73f0f2083","signature":"host-suspend-lapses-run-ownership-lease"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"provider-execution","diagnosis":"Recurring failure class: an interactive provider CLI (Claude Code TUI) launches with an expired credential, prints its auth banner ('Login expired \u00b7 Please run /login' / 'Not logged in'), performs zero work, and idles until the 90-minute session timeout \u2014 which then records a misleading 'timed_out' outcome and mints a failure investigation. Causal mechanism: interactive TUI providers bypass the provider-runner's typed error classification, the designed `CliProvider.authenticated` preflight hook has zero call sites, and the provider circuit breaker only sees HTTP-flavored auth failures \u2014 so consecutive auth-dead launches never trip anything and the orchestrator keeps feeding sessions into a dead provider serially. Observed cohort 2026-08-04T22:18Z\u21922026-08-05T02:53Z: #6463, #5980 (rework of PR #6893, this observation), #6991, #5336, plus the #5204 failure investigation \u2014 \u2265 5 \u00d7 90 min of capacity for zero output from one expired credential. Suggested fix: the typed provider readiness / auth-failure boundary already designed in open issue #6999 \u2014 (1) provider-owned cheap auth probe at launch, (2) launch control parks with a needs-human-style credential signal instead of spawning doomed sessions, (3) live-session early-output classification fails the session within minutes with a distinct non-timeout outcome. Any promotion of this signature should route to / dedup against #6999.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:37:50.154209+00:00","issue_number":7006,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"shipped","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7047","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7006"],"reason":"Provider-owned readiness and authentication classification now rejects expired credentials before a 90-minute zombie session.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:provider-auth-expired-zombie-session"}],"observation_ids":["20260805-124728Z:coding-1:A5","20260807-050245Z:coding-1:A4","20260807-070451Z:coding-1:A2"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"09dd486bf38846afab3cab7151daf4d4","signature":"provider-auth-expired-zombie-session"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"provider-execution","diagnosis":"## Causal mechanism\n\nWhen the coder role's provider account exhausts its quota, Claude Code does not exit and does not error on the control channel. It prints `You've hit your monthly spend limit` and drops into the interactive `/rate-limit-options` menu (`1. Stop and wait for limit to reset / 2. Add funds to continue with usage credits / 3. Switch to Team plan`). The process stays **alive**, the PTY stays **healthy**, the prompt was **accepted** \u2014 and no tokens will ever be produced.\n\n`persistent_session_exchange` classifies purely on the ABSENCE of output:\n\n```\nfailure_reason=prompt_not_accepted ... error=Agent did not produce terminal output or a response after prompt delivery for 120.1s\n```\n\nA quota wall and a dead PTY are identical under that predicate, so the transport remedy fires \u2014 `respawning in place and retrying the same turn (retry 1/1)` \u2014 and the respawned process hits the same wall on its first token. Each attempt costs a full 120 s timeout, two attempts exhaust the round, the round exhausts the exchange, and 3 consecutive exchange failures trip the `coder_no_completion` runaway halt. The halt path then drops the completion's publish actions and deletes the completion record, so a **billing condition destroys completed, validated work**.\n\nThe cost is asymmetric and invisible: the reviewer role runs a different provider (OpenAI Codex `gpt-5.6-sol` here), so it keeps returning valid verdicts while the coder is walled. The exchange therefore looks like a coder-quality problem rather than a provider outage, and the failure surfaces to the board as a generic `timed_out`.\n\n## Observation \u2014 issue #6971, 2026-08-09/10\n\n- Coder pair recording `/Users/brucegordon/dev/issue-orchestrator-6971/.issue-orchestrator/persistent-pairs/issue-6971/coder/terminal-recording.jsonl` contains the spend-limit message and `/rate-limit-options` modal twice \u2014 pid 3035, then respawned pid 20241.\n- `prompt_not_accepted` for issue=6971 at 15:03:19, 16:04:02, 19:03:55, 19:06:15, 19:18:43, 19:21:39, 19:42:39, 19:44:59 \u2014 a ~4h40m wall, four exchange sessions, zero coder turns completed.\n- **Account-level, not session-level:** `/Users/brucegordon/dev/issue-orchestrator-6858/.issue-orchestrator/persistent-pairs/issue-6858/coder/terminal-recording.jsonl` has the identical modal, and #6858's `prompt_not_accepted` lines land 3 seconds after #6971's (19:03:58, 19:06:18) in a different worktree.\n- Outcome: `Completion result: issue=6971 success=False actions=[]`, completion record deleted, `blocked-failed` applied, `e7508b3` (validated, 31 files, +1872/\u2212158) never pushed.\n- Broader incidence: `failure_reason=prompt_not_accepted` appears 37 times across 12 issues between 2026-08-04 and 2026-08-17 (6463, 5561, 5862, 5204, 7016, 6999, 6971, 6858, 7046, 7074, 6926). Not every one is quota, which is the point \u2014 one bucket is absorbing at least two causes with opposite correct remedies.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nGive the provider adapter a typed fact for *quota/limit exhaustion*, distinct from both auth failure and transport failure, recognised from the provider's own limit surface rather than from silence:\n\n1. **Classify, don't infer from silence.** Detect the spend-limit / rate-limit modal on the role's output stream and converge it to a typed `provider_quota_exhausted` outcome carrying the reset horizon when the provider states one. Silence alone must not mean `prompt_not_accepted`.\n2. **Never respawn into a wall.** A quota outcome must suppress the respawn+retry remedy entirely \u2014 it cannot succeed, and it converts a recoverable pause into an exhausted round budget.\n3. **Open the circuit, hold the work.** Route the outcome to `ProviderResilienceManager` as the sole circuit owner so affected roles pause instead of failing; the issue should become provider-unavailable (an owned, recoverable state) rather than `blocked-failed`.\n4. **Never let a provider outage reach a work-destroying verdict.** A quota-caused exchange failure must not count toward the `coder_no_completion` runaway budget, and must not drop a completion whose validation passed.\n\nThis is the same *shape* as #7042 ([P0-013] convert provider disconnects / interactive prompts into typed retryable infrastructure outcomes) and belongs on that seam. It is NOT #7006/#7021 (`provider-auth-expired-zombie-session`): there the credential is invalid; here the credential is valid and the account is out of budget, which needs a different fact, a different remedy, and a human-visible billing signal.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:38:31.847870+00:00","issue_number":7083,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"shipped","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7098","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7083"],"reason":"Provider quota exhaustion is now a typed human-fixable outage and does not consume retry rounds as prompt failure.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:provider-quota-exhausted-modal-misclassified-as-prompt-not-accepted"}],"observation_ids":["20260817-085803Z:coding-1:A2"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"012030761a60438399069646369fbc0f","signature":"provider-quota-exhausted-modal-misclassified-as-prompt-not-accepted"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"review-exchange","diagnosis":"","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:37:33.388669+00:00","issue_number":6913,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"superseded","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7179","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7198","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/6913"],"reason":"Validated coder work now enters durable escrow and recovery instead of being destroyed when review cannot complete.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:review-exchange-coder-no-completion"}],"observation_ids":["20260807-081053Z:coding-1:A3","20260807-083937Z:coding-1:A4","20260817-073208Z:coding-1:A8","20260817-085803Z:coding-1:A3","legacy:d97a43b73e594a9c:5"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"93850f3ceee94364b9be5f4689ed9be1","signature":"review-exchange-coder-no-completion"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"review-exchange","diagnosis":"Causal mechanism (observed on #5204, rounds 8-10): during round 8 the coder checked out a parent commit to A/B-test a flaky integration test and returned with HEAD detached at the branch tip 7913b02. Round 9's review was unaffected \u2014 it validated matching head 7913b027 and raised the new substantive F7/A5 finding \u2014 but the round-9 coder's F7/A5 fix commit and its validation record then landed on dangling commit 7add3460 while the session branch never moved. In round 10 the reviewer correctly rejected the evidence as F8 ('The claimed F7/A5 fix and passing validation exist on 7add3460, but the reviewed worktree is still 7913b027'), re-raised F7 (still present in the reviewed tree), and also found the independent new F9 defect (private-implementation imports in the fix's contract tests). The coder's round-10 recovery (branch fast-forwarded onto 7add3460, F9 addressed, attached clean HEAD 900b551b, full make validate green) was accepted as a valid response three minutes before the halt \u2014 max-round semantics give the coder the final turn, so no reviewer round remained to confirm it. Scope of this pattern: the detachment was a contributing evidence-integrity failure, not the sole cause of budget exhaustion \u2014 the independently discovered F9 would have required the round-10 rework regardless, and the final-coder-turn semantics meant a last-round fix could never be confirmed (that strand mechanism is case file #7012's subject, flagged separately). Suggested fix (code, review-exchange): the round runner should assert, before dispatching a coder result to the reviewer, that (a) the coder worktree HEAD is attached to the session branch and (b) the validation record's head_sha equals the branch tip being handed to the reviewer; on mismatch, fail the round immediately back to the coder with the precise discrepancy. This is a fail-fast guardrail that prevents a detached coder HEAD and mismatched branch-tip evidence from ever reaching the reviewer \u2014 here it would have bounced the round-9 coder result at acceptance time, sparing the reviewer attention spent on F8 in round 10; it does not claim the exchange would then have converged within budget. Implementation should reuse the existing reviewer-worktree branch-ownership and validation-evidence owners rather than adding a parallel check path. Evidence: round-10-coder-attempt-1.result.json (coder's own root-cause statement), round-9-reviewer-attempt-1.review-decision.json (matching-head validation plus new F7/A5 \u2014 no mismatch rejection in round 9), round-10-reviewer-attempt-1.review-decision.json (F7/F8/F9), orchestrator-tail.log 15:20:37 (round-10 response accepted response_type=ok) vs 15:20:48 (halt accepted).","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:38:06.355818+00:00","issue_number":7017,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"shipped","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7188","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7017"],"reason":"Publication and review custody are fenced to the exact validated head across Git and GitHub.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:review-exchange-detached-head-invalidates-review-evidence"}],"observation_ids":["20260807-042159Z:coding-1:A3"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"b4c0cdb2eb8848cb86259a64e0669639","signature":"review-exchange-detached-head-invalidates-review-evidence"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"review-exchange","diagnosis":"Causal mechanism: when a review exchange exhausts its round budget without reviewer approval, the session is finalized as failed and the failure reason surfaces as generic 'timed_out'. The coder's completion record (outcome=completed, requested_actions=[push_branch, create_pr, post_comment]) and a green validation record already exist at that point, but completion processing drops them: failure-diagnostic shows actions_taken=[] with errors=['review_exchange: stopped (max_rounds_exceeded)']. The branch is never pushed, so validated work exists only in the local worktree, and the misleading 'timed_out' label routes the issue into failure investigation instead of salvage.\n\nObserved instances (both 2026-08-04/05): #5204 \u2014 validation.passed=true, 14 commits local-only, exchange stopped max_rounds_exceeded (run 20260804-123846Z__coding-1, failure-diagnostic-20260804-192048.json); #5561 \u2014 validation passed in three run dirs, 34 commits local-only, 10 rounds each ending changes_requested while coder feedback was 'ok' (session review-exchange-5561-20260805T124615500797Z).\n\nSuggested fix (code): on max_rounds_exceeded with a completed+validated completion record, (1) record a distinct outcome (e.g. review_non_convergence) instead of timed_out, (2) push the branch and park the issue needs-human with the reviewer's final objections and the artifact pair attached for salvage, and (3) cap ping-pong earlier: a round where the coder reports 'ok' but the reviewer repeats changes_requested N times in a row is non-convergence, not progress. Distinct from case file #6913 (coder-no-completion): here the coder completed and validation passed \u2014 the round limit itself destroys the outcome.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:37:58.271357+00:00","issue_number":7012,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"superseded","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7183","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7198","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7012"],"reason":"Review exhaustion now preserves validated work in escrow and exposes an explicit recovery path.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:review-exchange-max-rounds-strands-validated-work"}],"observation_ids":["20260807-034116Z:coding-1:A4","20260807-042159Z:coding-1:A2","20260807-081053Z:coding-1:A2","20260807-083937Z:coding-1:A3"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"9dc2c68e61d44a49b399794abe519974","signature":"review-exchange-max-rounds-strands-validated-work"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"review-exchange","diagnosis":"## Causal mechanism\n\nWhen an exchange fails on the CODER side, the orchestrator restarts the whole exchange rather than resuming it. The restart begins at `round_index=1` with a fresh reviewer against the same unchanged head SHA. The previous reviewer's completed verdict \u2014 already written to `review-exchange/turns/round-1-reviewer-attempt-1.result.json` and `.review-report.md`, and already recorded in the timeline as `review_exchange.role_feedback` \u2014 is not consulted, not reused, and not published anywhere durable. It is simply re-derived, at full reviewer cost, and the prior copy is left to die with the worktree.\n\nThis is the same defect class as the one #6971 exists to fix (a completed piece of analysis leaves no durable disposition, so the next pass re-spends budget re-deriving it), expressed on the review surface instead of the investigation surface.\n\n## Observation \u2014 issue #6971, 2026-08-09/10\n\nFour reviewer passes, all on `head_sha e7508b330d712e83c405b2046f5dcd1d86c69d20`, all `validation_passed: true`, all `completed_rounds: 1`:\n\n| run dir | verdict at | report |\n|---|---|---|\n| `20260809-154726Z__review-exchange-6971-...` | 2026-08-09T22:04:02Z | 56 lines, F1\u2013F5 + A1\u2013A2 |\n| `20260810-005318Z__review-exchange-6971-...` | 2026-08-10T01:06:16Z | 44 lines, F1\u2013F4 + A1 |\n| `20260810-010830Z__review-exchange-6971-...` | 2026-08-10T01:21:40Z | 55 lines, F1\u2013F4 + A1\u2013A2 |\n| `20260810-012800Z__review-exchange-6971-...` | 2026-08-10T01:44:59Z | 72 lines, F1\u2013F4 + A1\u2013A2 |\n\nFour substantive, largely convergent reviews of the same diff. None was published to the issue or a PR; none was carried into the next attempt; all four survive only inside a worktree that `cleanup.with_tech_lead.remove_worktrees: true` is configured to delete.\n\nThe waste compounds with the provider-quota wall that caused the restarts (`provider-quota-exhausted-modal-misclassified-as-prompt-not-accepted`): the reviewer's provider was healthy, so every retry successfully spent reviewer budget to re-reach a conclusion that was already correct and already recorded.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nMake a completed reviewer verdict a durable, addressable fact keyed by `(issue, head_sha, round_index)`:\n\n1. On restart, if a verdict already exists for the unchanged head SHA, **resume from it** instead of re-running the reviewer.\n2. Publish a completed verdict out of the run dir \u2014 to the issue/PR or a retained artifact store \u2014 so it survives worktree cleanup (related: #7068 retain/pin run-scoped evidence independently of worktree cleanup).\n3. When an exchange is abandoned, attach the last completed review report to the issue so the rework agent inherits the findings rather than commissioning them again.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"1970-01-01T00:00:00+00:00","issue_number":7084,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"active","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7141","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7084"],"reason":"Review evidence is retained, but reuse of a completed verdict for an unchanged head still needs direct verification before retirement.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:review-exchange-restart-rederives-reviewer-verdict"}],"observation_ids":["20260817-085803Z:coding-1:A4"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"migration:137c59dbe6be9ba3","signature":"review-exchange-restart-rederives-reviewer-verdict"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"","diagnosis":"","fix_class":""},"expires_at":"1970-01-01T00:00:00+00:00","issue_number":7235,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"active","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7235"],"reason":"The case was freshly reconciled from accumulated sightings and its underlying API-budget tracker remains active.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:search-api-budget-exhaustion"}],"observation_ids":["6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:registration","6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:duplicate-6966","6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:duplicate-6977"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"migration:f449649b90464eca","signature":"search-api-budget-exhaustion"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"","diagnosis":"","fix_class":""},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:38:43.656679+00:00","issue_number":7236,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"superseded","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7191","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7215","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7236"],"reason":"The retained-work recovery stack now discovers, publishes, and exposes stranded validated branches through one durable owner.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:stranded-branch-recovery"}],"observation_ids":["6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:registration","6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:duplicate-6959","6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:duplicate-6970","6989-standing-problems-2026-08:case-file-reconciliation:duplicate-6973"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"f13e628f3e64417b85ae34e559d3038d","signature":"stranded-branch-recovery"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"stuck-sweep","diagnosis":"","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:37:42.208969+00:00","issue_number":6927,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"shipped","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7178","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/6927"],"reason":"Tech Lead investigations now require durable follow-through, preventing completed diagnoses from returning as unowned ghost failures.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:stuck-sweep-ghost-failure-reinjection"}],"observation_ids":["20260807-115108Z:coding-1:A2","20260807-125349Z:coding-1:A2","20260817-073208Z:coding-1:A10","legacy:8cb968d9241d8368:4"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"d5f886cd8c134c738bee083d1b09ce60","signature":"stuck-sweep-ghost-failure-reinjection"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-20147","classification":{"area":"stuck-sweep","diagnosis":"**Signature:** an open issue carries a blocking label (typically `blocked-failed`) while its own open PR is labelled for code review. The review scanner refuses the PR because the issue is blocked. The stuck sweep then treats the issue as unowned and re-injects it into failure investigation as a fabricated `timed_out`, where the only automatic remedies discard or duplicate the published work.\n\n**Causal mechanism**\n1. `review_validity.evaluate_review_validity` returns `issue_blocked` for any blocking label on the linked issue, so `PRScanner.scan_for_reviews` never queues the PR.\n2. `stuck_sweep._scan_stuck_issues` counts an issue as owned only through an allow-list: active session, pending tech-lead work, tech-lead-needs-human marker, open provider circuit, or disposition ledger. An open PR awaiting review is not on it, so the issue is a candidate.\n3. `stuck_sweep._recovered_failure` hard-codes `failure_reason=timed_out`, even when no session ever ran.\n4. In the investigation, `reset_retry` (authority `execute`) discards the PR, and operator Retry strips `pr-pending` (`retry_policy.py:21`) and relaunches coding. `recover_validated_work` needs a validated-work record, which a PR published by any other route does not have.\n\n**Observations:** porchpin, 2026-09-23 (8 green PRs, fixed only for the halted-exchange path by #7295). #7316 / PR #7317, 2026-09-26: reached by a non-halt route, zero sessions, and `observed_at == last_stuck_sweep_at`.\n\n**Suggested fix (code, stuck-sweep):** treat an issue whose open PR carries the review label and no PR-level blocker as owned by a release-to-review path instead of failure investigation. That path clears the issue's blocking label and keeps `pr-pending`, so the scanner queues the review. `reset_retry` and operator Retry must refuse while such a PR exists unless the operator explicitly abandons it. Derive the re-injected failure reason from real session evidence (`no_session` here) instead of `timed_out`. Point-fix tracker: #7293. The seam-level redesign is proposed separately (stuck-sweep ownership model). Findings T1, T2, T4.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-27T01:22:40.263425+00:00","issue_number":7319,"lifecycle":[],"observation_ids":["20260927-005628Z-d5599e144f4c4c2d85f5ddad05385cba:coding-1:A3"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"875eea1206174bc98dbc75e42cd9aa78","signature":"stuck-sweep-reinjects-green-pr-awaiting-review"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"tech-lead-authority","diagnosis":"**Signature:** a tech-lead run completes, its decision is deferred behind a\nreview exchange armed over a zero-commit branch, and the run's artifacts are then\ndestroyed by terminal cleanup before the exchange can converge.\n\n**Causal mechanism**\n\n`shape_requested_actions_for_tech_lead`\n(`control/tech_lead_session_policy.py:150-161`) drops only `POST_COMMENT`, so\n`CREATE_PR` rides on every tech-lead completion. `prepare_review_exchange`\n(`control/completion_review_exchange.py:254`) arms on `CREATE_PR in\nrequested_actions` with no commit check, and it runs from `_execute_actions`\n(`completion_processor.py:1662`) before any planned action. The deferral\n(`completion_processor.py:890`) then returns before the decision is applied, and\nthe zero-commit escape hatch (`completion_processor.py:1826`) sits downstream of\nthat return, unreachable. The completion record is left on disk so a later\nobservation can re-enter the pipeline - which makes the decision's survival\ndepend entirely on the worktree surviving, and terminal cleanup does not\nguarantee that.\n\n**Occurrence (#6926, run 4)**\n\nCompleted 04:29:45Z with `findings=4 proposed_actions=5`; deferred at 04:29:46Z;\n**coder** worktree removed 06:37:48Z by the ownership-loss terminal path, which\ndid not cancel the exchange; the **reviewer** checkout separately reclaimed by the\npair registry's release hook at 07:50:59Z, which did not stop the owning job; the\nexchange died 07:58:52Z with `FileNotFoundError` and its background job failed\n07:59:10Z; the completion record was never restored. Zero GitHub effect from ~1h of\nagent time, and a fifth investigation launched at 07:32:15Z to re-derive the same\ndiagnosis.\n\n**Suggested fix**\n\nGate exchange arming on \"is there anything to publish?\" above\n`prepare_review_exchange`, with one owner shared by the publish-shaping and\narming paths; and make decision application survive worktree loss by preserving\nthe completion record and artifact pair outside the worktree at terminal time.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"2026-09-16T01:38:15.977809+00:00","issue_number":7081,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"shipped","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7173","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7176","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/pull/7178","https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7081"],"reason":"Clean Tech Lead decisions no longer require code publication, and all launches and follow-through now have durable custody.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:tech-lead-decision-deferred-into-review-exchange-then-destroyed"}],"observation_ids":["20260817-073208Z:coding-1:A7","20260820-010159Z:coding-1:A6"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"4644f646b0484d7d8ced8bfdd2962fde","signature":"tech-lead-decision-deferred-into-review-exchange-then-destroyed"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-90186","classification":{"area":"tech-lead-authority","diagnosis":"Causal mechanism: the #6878 dedup gate routes a verified duplicate_of onto the existing issue (CommentExisting) ONLY when the candidate is inside the session's IMMUTABLE launch-authority redirect grant (DuplicateTargetGrant). A failure investigation's grant is its focus issue alone, so EVERY duplicate_of accrual aimed at a pre-existing tracker fails the grant check and is gated: a NEW standalone issue is filed that preserves the candidate in a note. This is the gate working as designed \u2014 corpus membership proves the target exists, is open, and is an issue; it does NOT prove the session has authority to write there or that the claimed semantic relationship is valid, and CommentExisting is deliberately unrepresentable outside the immutable grant (never a capability synthesized at completion from untrusted input). The minted issues are therefore gated reconciliation candidates, not an authority defect. The systemic COST under investigation churn is still real: evidence intended to accrue quietly onto trackers becomes open issues a human must find and reconcile, and the stuck-sweep re-investigation loop (case file #6927) multiplies it \u2014 roughly 3 per redundant completed investigation. Observed 2026-08-07: the #5561 investigation (run 20260807-081053Z) proposed three accruals intended for #6960 (recovery-vs-timeout race), #6986 (unowned pair processes), and #7011 (salvage tracker); all three targets are open and present in the local open-issue corpus, yet \u2014 correctly, per the grant rule \u2014 the applier filed gated candidates #7027 / #7028 / #7029 (orchestrator.log 184758-184770, '[APPLIER] Created tech_lead issue ... for 0 PRs') with accrual-shaped titles ('Fresh timestamped occurrence #5561...', 'Salvage ground truth refresh #5561...'). Suggested fix (code, tech-lead authority/dedup seam) \u2014 bounded mechanisms that KEEP DuplicateTargetGrant as the sole authority owner and never treat corpus membership alone as authorization: (1) an operator-approved redirect lifecycle for gated candidates \u2014 the gated issue already preserves the candidate reference, so add an explicit approval surface (a human approves the redirect, mirroring the existing proposed-tech-lead label-removal approval shape) after which the ORCHESTRATOR merges the observation onto the verified target and closes the orphan; and/or (2) an orchestrator-DERIVED grant at launch: when composing a failure investigation's immutable launch authority, include the specific tracker issues the orchestrator ALREADY trusts as related from pre-session facts (e.g. the focus issue's open salvage tracker and the case files it selected as session inputs) \u2014 a trusted-facts extension of the same immutable grant, decided before the session, never from completion input. Reserve gating-as-new-issue for candidates outside that trusted set. Either mechanism restores quiet accrual for the common case while the authority boundary stays exactly where #6878 put it.","fix_class":"code"},"expires_at":"1970-01-01T00:00:00+00:00","issue_number":7037,"lifecycle":[{"disposition":"needs_human","evidence":["https://github.com/issue-orchestrator/issue-orchestrator/issues/7037"],"reason":"The authority boundary is intentional; the remaining choice between operator-approved redirects and launch-derived grants needs an explicit design decision.","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T23:15:00+00:00","transition_id":"7240-issue-orchestrator-case-files-2026-09:tech-lead-dedup-redirect-gate-orphans-offgrant-evidence"}],"observation_ids":["20260807-115108Z:coding-1:A4"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"migration:39850787ece46856","signature":"tech-lead-dedup-redirect-gate-orphans-offgrant-evidence"},{"claimant_id":"orchestrator-20147","classification":{"area":"","diagnosis":"","fix_class":""},"expires_at":"2026-09-27T01:22:56.260746+00:00","issue_number":7321,"lifecycle":[],"observation_ids":["20260927-005628Z-d5599e144f4c4c2d85f5ddad05385cba:coding-1:A5"],"pending":null,"pending_observation":null,"pending_retirement":null,"publication_started_at":null,"reservation_id":"d085dc7edfe749b08f162bb58d3439c6","signature":"tech-lead-evidence-blind-to-blocked-issue-open-pr"}],"version":2}